{
  "over-ons": {
    "eyebrow": "The company",
    "title": "About Tape Solutions",
    "lead": "A specialist in self-adhesive tapes and packaging materials, with a practical approach to applications, converting and private label.",
    "image": "bedrijfsgebouw.jpg",
    "alt": "Exterior of the Tape Solutions premises in Capelle aan den IJssel",
    "provenance": "source-facts-and-new-copy",
    "sections": [
      {
        "eyebrow": "Who we are",
        "title": "Materials knowledge with a direct point of contact",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Tape Solutions supplies self-adhesive tapes and packaging materials for professional use. On its original website, the company describes 16 years of trading experience and activity in industry, food and packaging, DIY and construction. These are the sectors from which we take our starting point, not a claim that every material is suitable for every application.",
          "The offering extends beyond standard materials. Tape Solutions also describes custom production, converting and private-label solutions, working with brands and wholesalers as well as businesses that need to discuss a specific application.",
          "The most useful first step is often a conversation about what needs to be joined, protected, sealed or packed. Substrate, dimensions, conditions and quantities can all affect which material or construction is worth considering."
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "How we work",
        "title": "From application to a practical next step",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Describe the task",
            "body": "Tell us what you want to seal, reinforce, protect or package and in which conditions it will be used."
          },
          {
            "title": "Share the requirements",
            "body": "If you already know the size, substrate, quantities or format, include these details. If not, start with the challenge."
          },
          {
            "title": "Explore the options",
            "body": "We discuss potentially suitable material groups, available product data and whether converting or a custom format is relevant."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "Working together",
        "title": "Why clear communication matters",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The original Tape Solutions website emphasises long-term relationships, open communication and mutual respect. Our enquiry process follows the same principle: explain the application, make the requirements clear and agree what information is needed next.",
          "Looking for a specific tape or packaging application? Visit the materials overview for orientation, or send us a message for a more detailed discussion."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cta": {
      "title": "Talk to Tape Solutions",
      "text": "Share your application and we can discuss a suitable next step.",
      "label": "Contact the team",
      "slug": "contact"
    }
  },
  "maatwerk": {
    "eyebrow": "Converting and private label",
    "title": "Custom tape and packaging solutions",
    "lead": "Discuss converting, non-standard dimensions, packaging applications and private-label requirements with Tape Solutions.",
    "image": "tape-converting-workstation.webp",
    "alt": "Illustrative tape converting workstation with rolls on a rewinding machine, not a photograph of the TPS Pack facility",
    "provenance": "source-facts-and-new-copy",
    "sections": [
      {
        "eyebrow": "Your application first",
        "title": "When a standard format is not the whole answer",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A suitable adhesive or packaging material depends on how it will be used. Tape Solutions describes custom production and converting alongside its standard assortment. A request can concern width, length, presentation, material construction or a private-label project. What is technically possible must be confirmed against the actual product and application.",
          "For example, an installer may need a tape format that is easier to apply on-site, while a packaging business may need a consistent material presentation for its own brand. The conversation starts with the intended use, not an assumed off-the-shelf specification."
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "Available directions",
        "title": "Topics to discuss",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Converting",
            "body": "Discuss slitting, rewinding or another appropriate material format, subject to technical feasibility and availability."
          },
          {
            "title": "Private label",
            "body": "Explore the possibility of packaging or presenting an agreed material under your own brand."
          },
          {
            "title": "Application advice",
            "body": "Share the substrate, environmental conditions, required dimensions and handling process for a focused discussion."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "Prepare your request",
        "title": "Five details that help us respond",
        "bullets": [
          "What needs to be joined, sealed, protected, wrapped or bundled?",
          "What material or surface will the product contact?",
          "What dimensions, roll format or packaging presentation do you need?",
          "Are temperature, moisture, storage or application conditions important?",
          "What approximate quantity and delivery location are relevant to your enquiry?"
        ],
        "paragraphs": [
          "You do not need every technical detail to get in touch. Tell us what is known and identify anything that still needs to be investigated. We will not confirm suitability, certification or delivery dates before the actual requirements are reviewed."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cta": {
      "title": "Have an application in mind?",
      "text": "Describe your requirements in the quotation form. Submitting the form does not place an order.",
      "label": "Request a quotation",
      "slug": "aanvraag"
    }
  },
  "toepassingen": {
    "eyebrow": "Applications",
    "title": "Tape and packaging materials by application",
    "lead": "Start with the job to be done, then compare relevant material groups and discuss the conditions that matter.",
    "image": "tape-converting-workstation.webp",
    "alt": "Illustrative industrial converting equipment used for tape formats and packaging applications",
    "provenance": "new-explanatory-copy",
    "sections": [
      {
        "eyebrow": "Practical orientation",
        "title": "What are you trying to do?",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Different tasks call for different materials. A tape used to finish insulation is selected for different reasons than a stretch film used to stabilise a pallet. Rather than assuming one product will work everywhere, identify the surface, the load, the process and the environment first.",
          "Use the examples below as a starting point. The product catalogue remains the source for actual names, variations and specifications."
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "Common use cases",
        "title": "Four application routes",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Sealing and insulation finishing",
            "body": "Consider the substrate, moisture, temperature and expected movement. Aluminium tapes and foil-related materials may be relevant to discuss.",
            "slug": "aluminium-tapes",
            "link": "Explore aluminium tapes"
          },
          {
            "title": "Reinforcing or securing packages",
            "body": "Packaging weight, tension and handling method influence the need for reinforced tape or strapping.",
            "slug": "omsnoeringsband",
            "link": "Explore strapping"
          },
          {
            "title": "Protecting palletised loads",
            "body": "Stretch film and cardboard edge protectors can help protect or stabilise loads; choose on the basis of the packing process.",
            "slug": "rekfolie",
            "link": "Explore stretch film"
          },
          {
            "title": "Construction and installation",
            "body": "Consider the surface and whether the task involves joining, masking, reinforcing or sealing.",
            "slug": "bouwtapes",
            "link": "Explore construction tapes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "eyebrow": "Choosing with care",
        "title": "Application questions worth asking",
        "bullets": [
          "What are the substrate and surface condition?",
          "Will application take place indoors or outdoors?",
          "Do temperature or moisture vary during use?",
          "Is the job manual, automated or part of a packaging line?",
          "Do you require a particular width, roll format or private-label presentation?"
        ],
        "paragraphs": [
          "Product suitability must always be checked against the relevant technical data and your actual conditions. If you are unsure where to start, send us a short description of the application."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cta": {
      "title": "Unsure which route fits?",
      "text": "We can help you narrow down the relevant questions before choosing a material.",
      "label": "Discuss your application",
      "slug": "maatwerk"
    }
  },
